From a302b894f2fbc83fb8c09bb2fe687913f4e5f7e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: God489 <360921522+God489@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 05:34:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 15/25] Shaders: lower v_ldexp_f32, v_frexp_*_f32,
 v_cvt_pknorm_*_f32 and 20 more VALU instructions

They decode but had no lowering, so any shader using one failed to translate. Each is lowered as the RDNA2 ISA defines it and checked on the hardware adapter and WARP against a reference: v_ldexp_f32 and v_frexp_mant/exp_f32 exactly in integers (a host that flushes denormals no longer matters), v_cvt_pknorm_i16/u16_f32 from the exact product, v_cvt_pk_u16_u32/i16_i32, v_cvt_off_f32_i4, v_mul_hi_u32_u24/i32_i24, v_mul_lo_i32, v_add/sub_nc_i32, v_sad_u8/hi_u8/u16/u32, v_lerp_u8 and the integer dot products. The clamp bit on v_add/sub/subrev_nc_u32 now saturates instead of failing translation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 7c6e1d4286d1b1eeeb3e539db7cd6f89608283d2)
